AB  - Real-Time Release Testing (RTRT) is an advanced pharmaceutical quality-assurance approach that enables product quality to be evaluated using real-time process data, in-process measurements, and validated analytical technologies. Unlike conventional end-product testing, RTRT focuses on building quality into the manufacturing process through continuous monitoring and control. The integration of Process Analytical Technology (PAT), Quality by Design (QbD), multivariate data analysis, automation, and advanced analytical techniques facilitates improved understanding and control of critical material attributes and critical process parameters. This review discusses the principles, implementation strategies, pharmaceutical applications, advantages, challenges, and regulatory aspects of RTRT. The major benefits include reduced testing time, faster batch disposition, improved process understanding, reduced product waste, enhanced manufacturing efficiency, and consistent product quality. However, implementation can be challenging due to high initial investment, instrument calibration and validation requirements, data integrity and cyber security concerns, skilled workforce requirements, regulatory expectations, and integration with legacy manufacturing systems. Regulatory frameworks from organizations such as the US Food and Drug Administration (FDA), European Medicines Agency (EMA), and International Council for Harmonisation (ICH) provide a scientific and risk-based foundation for implementing RTRT. Future developments involving Artificial Intelligence (AI), Machine Learning (ML), Digital Twins, Internet of Things (IoT), Big Data Analytics, and Industry 4.0 are expected to further enhance real-time quality monitoring and predictive manufacturing. RTRT therefore offers significant potential to modernize pharmaceutical manufacturing by enabling efficient, science-based, and continuous assurance of product quality.
